It looks like you're trying to access a property on an object that hasn't been initialized. In 'monitor.js', check if the variable you are accessing on line 42 is properly defined before usage.

Here's a possible fix:

```javascript
// src/monitor.js
if (monitorConfig && monitorConfig.interval) {
    setInterval(() => {
        checkUptime();
    }, monitorConfig.interval);
} else {
    console.error('Monitor configuration is invalid.');
}
```

Make sure to test this after implementing the fix.
